NAME
    id - print uid and gid

SYNOPSIS
    id

DESCRIPTION
    Calls SYS_GETUID and SYS_GETGID and prints them in the form

      uid=0(root) gid=0

    The user name is looked up by reading /etc/passwd and matching
    the uid; if no match is found, the (name) parenthetical is
    omitted.

EXAMPLES
    id

EXIT STATUS
    0   always

SEE ALSO
    login(1), passwd(5)

NOTES
    No -u / -g / -n flags. Multi-user support (session 47) gave
    every fork an inherited uid/gid; setuid switches it within
    the allowed envelope (root → anyone; non-root → no change).
